---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProjectCaseStudy from '../components/site/ProjectCaseStudy.astro';
import metadata from '../siteMetadata';
const project={name:'Dantian',web:true,logo:'/portfolio/dantian-logo.svg',title:'The practice behind the products.',summary:'I began practising Tai Chi and exploring Taoism in my early twenties. More than thirty years later, that practice runs through my teaching, my approach to design and the products I choose to build. Dantian gives the teaching a home on the web.',role:'Tai Chi teaching · Product design · Web development · Local search',website:'https://dantian.co.za/',hero:'/portfolio/dantian-teaching.webp',heroAlt:'James Godwin teaching with students during a Tai Chi practice',heroCaption:'Teaching through movement and attention. A photograph from the Dantian website.',sections:[
{label:'The beginning',title:'A practice I began in my early twenties.',paragraphs:['Tai Chi and Taoism have been part of my life since my early twenties. They became a continuing thread alongside my career in technology, giving me something to return to as the work, companies and responsibilities changed.','I trained directly under Grandmaster Dr Lin Feng-Chao, a closed-door disciple of Cheng Man-Ching. That lineage gave me a practical way to explore relaxation, structure and attention through movement. The learning continues each time I practise or teach.'],links:[{href:'/taoism',label:'My Tai Chi and Taoist background'}]},
{label:'What carries into the work',title:'Notice where the effort is going.',paragraphs:['In Tai Chi, I keep returning to tension, timing and unnecessary effort. Those questions follow me into product work. Where is someone struggling? What are they being asked to hold in their head? Which step is making a simple task harder than it needs to be?','For me, designing an interface and practising Tai Chi draw on the same habit of paying attention. I try to understand what is happening before adding more, then find a clearer way through. My philosophy page explores that relationship in more detail.'],links:[{href:'/philosophy',label:'The practice behind my judgement'}]},
{label:'The teaching website',title:'Help someone take their first step.',paragraphs:['Dantian brings my teaching and practice resources together. Someone finding Tai Chi for the first time needs a clear introduction, a way to understand the teaching and practical information about joining a class. Returning students need somewhere to continue exploring.','I designed and built the website around those needs, connecting local class pages with teaching background, the Short Form, videos, books and practice resources. Local search work helps people looking for Tai Chi in Sedgefield and the Garden Route find a relevant place to begin.','The website carries the current class information and enquiry routes. Keeping those details there gives visitors one place to check arrangements and get in touch.'],links:[{href:'https://dantian.co.za/',label:'Visit the teaching website'}]},
{label:'Practice together',title:'A little room to notice.',paragraphs:['At JUMO, teaching colleagues at lunchtime led me to create Just Being for our engineers. I wanted to share a practical way to notice tension and find a little room before reacting.','That work continues through Return to Stillness, a one hour, one to one session exploring breath, posture and attention. Stillness Under Pressure brings the same practice into working life through workshops for teams. Neither requires any Tai Chi experience.'],links:[{href:'/return-to-stillness',label:'Return to Stillness · One to one'},{href:'/workshops',label:'Stillness Under Pressure · For teams'}]},
{label:'From practice to products',title:'Different expressions of the same background.',paragraphs:['The products I build grow out of this background too. The connection is clear in several of them. Taoist Breath supports practice between classes, Between Breaths creates a small pause in the day, and True Essence brings reflection, guided practice and writing together.','AI Ching grew from years of collecting and reading I Ching translations. GratefulFor makes room for appreciation, while Harmonic Echo explores a creative pause through humming and generative art. Each has its own purpose, but attention, curiosity and the space to notice are recurring interests.','Even my practical work tools begin with noticing a repeated difficulty in my own day. This long-standing practice shapes what I care about and how I choose to work.'],links:[{href:'/work/taoist-breath',label:'Taoist Breath'},{href:'/work/between-breaths',label:'Between Breaths'},{href:'/work/true-essence',label:'True Essence'},{href:'/work/ai-ching',label:'AI Ching'},{href:'/work/gratefulfor',label:'GratefulFor'},{href:'/work/harmonic-echo',label:'Harmonic Echo'}]},
{label:'Still practising',title:'Teaching, making and returning.',paragraphs:['Dantian is part of the same life as the software work. Teaching gives me a place to share what I have learned, and a reason to keep looking closely at the simple things.','The website is one expression of that. The books, reflective products and ongoing practice are others. Together they show more of the background behind the person designing and building the work in this portfolio.'],links:[{href:'/books',label:'Books and daily reflections'},{href:'/taoism',label:'Explore the practice'}]}
]};
const pageMetadata={...metadata.defaultMetadata,title:'Dantian | James Godwin',description:project.summary,path:'/dantian',url:metadata.siteUrl+'/dantian'};
---
<SiteLayout metadata={pageMetadata} current="work"><ProjectCaseStudy project={project}/></SiteLayout>
